# Core Standards (Always-On)

These rules apply to every project using this repository.

## Language & Formatting
- Prefer clear, explicit code over clever shortcuts.
- Use consistent naming: nouns for data, verbs for actions.
- Keep files focused; avoid multi-purpose "kitchen sink" modules.

## Security & Performance Guardrails
- Never introduce insecure defaults (e.g., hard-coded secrets, open CORS, unsafe eval).
- Validate all external inputs at boundaries.
- Prefer efficient algorithms; avoid O(n^2) patterns when scalable alternatives exist.

## Architectural Boundaries
- Separate domain logic from UI/framework glue.
- Keep side effects isolated behind well-defined interfaces.
- Avoid tight coupling between layers; use clear contracts.

## Hard Prohibitions (AI Must NEVER)
- Do not add telemetry, tracking, or data collection without explicit user approval.
- Do not auto-modify configuration or policy files without confirmation.
- Do not invent requirements or implement speculative features.
